Default the BeaglePlay U-Boot environment to silent=1

CONFIG_SILENT_CONSOLE (enabled via uboot-fragments.cfg) only silences
the console once the 'silent' env var is set to a non-empty value —
it doesn't change the default. Without this, U-Boot proper still
prints its full banner and boot-progress lines to the 115200 UART on
every boot. Set it in the board's default environment so it's silent
from the very first boot with no runtime setenv step required.
CONFIG_SILENT_U_BOOT_ONLY (also in uboot-fragments.cfg) keeps this
scoped to U-Boot itself, so the kernel's own console/earlycon is
unaffected — see SETUP-BEAGLEPLAY.md for why that still needs to work.

--- a/board/beagle/beagleplay/beagleplay.env
+++ b/board/beagle/beagleplay/beagleplay.env
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include <env/ti/mmc.env>

 name_kern=Image
+silent=1
 console=ttyS2,115200n8
 args_all=setenv optargs ${optargs} earlycon=ns16550a,mmio32,0x02800000
 run_kern=booti ${loadaddr} ${rd_spec} ${fdtaddr}
